  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans:\r\rSite Location Plan 12.08.2025\rExisting and Proposed Block Plan EP001 25.02.2025\rProposed Floor Plans P001 05.08.2025\rProposed Elevations P002 05.08.2025\rProposed Elevations P003 05.08.2025\rProposed Section P004 05.08.2025\rHighway Safety Impact Form\rSuDS Pro Forma\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The external finishing materials shall match those used in the construction of the existing building and/or areas of hard surfacing.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the cycle parking indicated within the supporting information, prior to occupation, unless otherwise agreed, cycle parking should be provided in compliance with the following criteria:\r\r- Provision of a minimum of SEVEN long stay cycle parking spaces, one per HMO bedroom.\r\r- In an accessible location: The access route to the cycle parking enclosures should be of sufficient wide to enable the bike to enter the store. \r\rSuch facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision and availability of adequate cycle parking.\r",
    "The development shall not be fully occupied until refuse and waste storage and recycling facilities have been provided within the curtilage of the application site as required by the standards of the Council. Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the occupiers of adjoining premises; protect the general environment; prevent any obstruction to pedestrian movement and to ensure that there are adequate facilities for the storage and recycling of recoverable materials.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 7 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen and dining/living rooms shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r"
  ],
